2026-09-27T04:47:47.8787502Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8787932Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8788497Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8788935Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8789127Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8789507Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8789732Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8790018Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8790678Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8791041Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8791251Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8791785Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8792115Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8792347Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8793029Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8793819Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8794929Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8795827Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8796038Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8796756Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8797658Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8798165Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8798639Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8799324Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8799515Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8799904Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8800092Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8802206Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8805030Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8805489Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8806438Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8807379Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8808503Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8809618Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8811584Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8812122Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8812856Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8813480Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8813850Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8815897Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8818287Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8819589Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8821318Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:47.8821744Z 
